PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
  • 8 GlassPanels (web L1307/1361/1414/1454/1512/1659/1880/2183) -> 8 HIG cards via .regularMaterial
    (ADR-005). Charts/maps: NONE in the web source.
  • Data: the 4 queries (useAlertRules/useNotificationChannels/useVehicles/useAlertMetrics) + 7
    mutations (save/delete/toggle/snooze/test/bulkEnable/bulkDisable) bind through the P1/S8
    AlertStudioSource seam; no HTTP in the view. The 11 web hook names are preserved at the call
    sites (useAlertMetrics->metrics, useSaveAlertRule->save, useToggleAlertRule->toggle, ...).
  • All editor logic ported + unit-asserted: signal-type inference, operator allow-list coercion,
    value-kind resolution, the force-choose tri-state, escalation higher-severity rule, canSave.
  • i18n: i18next `{{token}}` interpolation is rendered as the Foundation-native positional `%@`
    (NSLocalizedString + String(format:)) — the platform-correct equivalent; KEY NAMES match the web
    1:1 (125/125 referenced in .swift, verified). 13 `*Placeholder` key references carry the scanner's
    sanctioned `// parity:allow` marker (the web's input-placeholder keys are parity-required, not stubs).
  • a11y: every panel/row is a combined VoiceOver element; the enable/once affordances carry web `title`
    tooltips via `.help()`; Dynamic Type + light/dark + increased-contrast via the design tokens.
  • Navigation: the existing AppRouteParser already resolves /notifications/studio -> .notifications via
    its first-segment match; the page registers at .notifications (the only notifications page built).

